  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S. Hiriya Someshwara Industries And ... vs The Union Of India And Ors on 26 April, 2019 Author: P.B.Bajanthri Bench: P.B.Bajanthri 1 In The High Court Of Karnataka Kalabragi Bench Dated This The 26Th Day Of April, 2019 Before The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice P.B.Bajanthri W.P.Nos.205787 And 206152-153/2016 (Lb-Res) Between: 1. M/s Hiriya Someshwara Industries, Plot No.168, D1 and D168, Sy.No.109, Growth Centre, Dist. Raichur - 580 134. 2. M/s Padmashree Acqua Industries, Mpl No.12-10-38, Utkur Complex, Siyatalab, Gunj Road, Raichur - 584 101. 3. M/ s Maruti Industries, Through its Proprietor Sri G.Jagannath Reddy S/o G.Rama Reddy, Plot No.169, 170, Sy.No.11/2, Raichur Growth Center, Industrial Area, Chikkasugur Hobli, Raichur - 584 134. ... Petitioners (By Sri Manvendra Reddy, Advocate) And: 1. The Union of India, Through Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, 2 M/S. Hiriya Someshwara Industries And ... vs The Union Of India And Ors on 26 April, 2019",
    "facts": "ORDER In these petitions, petitioners have assailed Annexure-E proceedings of respondent No.5 vide No.g/Evg/Dg/14-15 and agreement dated 09.06.2015. 2 2. Petitioners and sixth respondent are into purified drinking water business. Fifth respondent in terms of policy for providing pure drinking water to the people of the jurisdiction of fifth respondent proceeded to award contract to the sixth respondent for installation of water purifying units at the respective places stated by the fifth respondent. Accordingly, fifth respondent has entered into agreement for a period of five years for 12 units in different wards as is evident from Annexures 'E' and 'F'. No doubt such agreement executed by fifth respondent with the sixth respondent is not for any monitory gain by the fifth respondent. Therefore, question of inviting tender and other process to commence water purifying units at identified places in the respective wards of fifth respondent is territorial jurisdiction. Sixth respondent after installation of water purifier units at the respective places he is charging certain amount to the general public to supply purified drinking water. Such an act is nothing but providing service through fifth respondent.",
    "arguments": "5. Supreme Court in the case of Tata Cellular vs. Union of India, reported in (1994) 6 Supreme Court Cases 651 held as under : \"70. It cannot be denied that the principles of judicial review would apply to the exercise of contractual powers by Government bodies in order to prevent arbitrariness or favoritism. Government is the guardian of the finances of the State.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "5. Supreme Court in the case of Tata Cellular vs. Union of India, reported in (1994) 6 Supreme Court Cases 651 held as under : \"70. It cannot be denied that the principles of judicial review would apply to the exercise of contractual powers by Government bodies in order to prevent arbitrariness or favoritism. Government is the guardian of the finances of the State."
